= Bristol Meets With Staal

Otto Bristol, former Minister-President of Heartland and leader of our reformist wing, has—without informing the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> leadership—met privately with Chancellor von Staal. Bristol proposed cooperation, on the condition that Staal relinquish federal control over Heartland and restore him to office with full authority, including the power to dissolve the state Assembly. Bristol suggested that, together, they could rule by decree and wage a determined campaign against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span>.

Staal, however, was unenthusiastic. Having led the Heartland coup himself, he is reluctant to undo the federal consolidation of power. More importantly, unlike Bristol, he is not committed to weakening the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>; he still views them as a potential source of support for his cabinet—admiring the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**SA**</span>’s militarism and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>’s fanatical discipline as traits to be co-opted into the state.

